From cce992a1e7a2a4fa0ff21a409e475c039ada02dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: taekim <taekim@day34.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 00:05:11 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 10/39] Put a drawing's points through its own matrix, keep the
 picture inside it, and stop filling a line
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three defects in the shape export, each measured on the same manual.

A drawing's points are stored in the object's original space and the shape's six
render coefficients are what place them — the renderer applies them and this
export did not, so a pair of real arrows came out as "M 0,0 L 100,100", 1pt
specks that carried none of their extent.

A shape that CONTAINS pictures is a screenshot in a frame: exporting the frame
and dropping the picture left three consecutive pages as an empty red rectangle.
The picture is the content, so it is what ships, and the frame's box no longer
reserves a second empty one below it.

And a line record still carries a fill — white, in these files — so filling any
path painted white bars over the text; a table's own column label disappeared
under one. Only a path that closes is filled now.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/document_core/queries/document_json.rs | 116 ++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 100 insertions(+), 16 deletions(-)

